---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Cookie Policy" description="Essential website technologies and your analytics and advertising choices.">
  <section class="section"><div class="container legal-copy"><h1 class="section-title">Cookie Policy</h1><p>Last updated: 29 October 2026.</p><h2>Your choices</h2><p>The site uses an opt-out measurement setup. Google Analytics and Google Ads measurement run automatically unless you have rejected them. Accept keeps measurement enabled. Reject stops it and remembers your choice. You can change your choice using Cookie settings in the footer.</p><button class="btn btn-secondary" type="button" data-cookie-settings>Change cookie settings</button>
<h2>Essential technologies</h2><p>We remember your measurement choice in browser storage for 180 days. The preference cookie <code>ses_tracking</code> also remembers rejection when localStorage is unavailable. A saved rejection from our previous notice is honoured. After a preference expires or is cleared, the notice is shown again.</p><p>Cloudflare Turnstile runs on pages containing enquiry forms to help distinguish genuine submissions from abuse. It processes browser and interaction information and may use security-related browser technologies. Vercel may also process request and security information to provide hosting and protect the site. These services are not used by this site's code for advertising.</p>
<h2>Website analytics</h2><p>Unless rejected, Google Analytics 4 measures page visits, navigation clicks, scroll depth, form starts and successful enquiries, together with browser and device information. This helps us understand how people move through the site and which pages are the last recorded in a visit. Analytics may set first-party cookies such as <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code>. We do not record session videos or collect the contents of enquiry fields through analytics.</p>
<h2>Advertising measurement</h2><p>Unless rejected, Google Ads measures visits and interactions such as phone clicks and successful enquiries. It may use first-party cookies with names beginning <code>_gcl_</code> and Google-managed advertising technologies. Only successful enquiry submissions trigger our enquiry conversion; a phone click or form start is not counted as a completed enquiry. Exact cookies and expiry depend on Google's configuration and your browser. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/cookies">Google's cookie information</a>.</p><p>Our tracking code does not send names, email addresses, phone numbers or enquiry messages. Accepting measurement does not subscribe you to email marketing.</p>
<h2>Rejection and browser controls</h2><p>Reject stops optional measurement, clears accessible first-party Google measurement cookies and reloads the page to unload Google's code. Rejection prevents future tracking; it cannot undo information already sent. We cannot directly delete cookies stored on Google's own domains; use your browser controls to remove those. Interactions after rejection are not replayed if you accept later.</p><p>You can clear cookies and site storage using your browser settings. Read our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for further information.</p>
<!-- OWNER: verify the final deployed cookie inventory, including Vercel firewall and Turnstile settings, before publication. --></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .legal-copy { max-width: 850px; }
  h2 { margin-top: 2rem; font-size: 1.4rem; }
  p, li { line-height: 1.75; }
  a { text-decoration: underline; }
</style>
